tip: | Look at the curve. | Follow the top edge from the tip down one side. The edge is drawn in runs of pixels, and it looks smooth because their lengths change in order.
tip: 1 | Count the runs. | From the top: 8, 3, 2, then 1 again and again. Then the edge turns and the runs go down, 1, 2 and longer. A run that breaks that order is a jaggy.
tip: | Try it. | With the Pencil, add one pixel on top of the curve. One run out of order shows as a bump at once. Undo it and the curve is smooth again. | pencil
